+# Swarm architecture
+
+[Français](../architecture/OVERVIEW.md) · [Repository overview](../../README.en.md)
+
+Overview reviewed on **October 23, 2026**. It connects components to their
+contracts; specialized documents retain the detailed requirements.
+**Rust porting is partial.** A module, command or local proof does not establish
+qualification of its complete journey or cutover of the user service. The
+[migration status](RUST-MIGRATION.md) and [active plan, FR](../plans/migration-rust/PLAN.md)
+retain outstanding criteria.
+
+## Responsibilities and boundaries
+
+[![Logical architecture, pending identity integration and future confinement](../diagrams/architecture-overview-en.svg)](../diagrams/architecture-overview-en.svg)
+
+[Open at full size](../diagrams/architecture-overview-en.svg) · [Mermaid source](../diagrams/architecture-overview-en.mmd)
+
+| Layer | Responsibility | Boundary to preserve |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Human | Objective, permissions, limits and decisions within their authority | Adoption does not start execution; a local identity does not attest a human identity |
+| AI supervision | Plan, decompose, assess progress and decide next steps | The root supervisor owns the overall objective; scope owners stay within their scope |
+| Deterministic engine | Durable state, observations, dependencies, reservations, budgets and authorized application | The engine checks the contract; agent prose creates no authority |
+| Execution | Launch and monitor attempts and provider tools | Process completion, report delivery and acceptance remain distinct |
+| Verification | Checks, evidence freshness and candidate review | Independent candidate review and global cycle judgment are separate contracts |
+| Context | Instructions, requirements, references and selected memory versions | Received context retains provenance; it grants no authority |
+| Public access | Supported CLI operations and HTTP routes | An implemented CLI operation does not establish HTTP or web parity |
+
+Application-level permission and path checks do not establish OS confinement of
+a hostile provider. Running the control service under a separate OS account and
+mandatory access mediation belong to the [deferred AC-02 work](plans/actions-confiance/securite-execution-apex.md).
+
+## Native code organization
+
+The [Cargo workspace](../../rust/Cargo.toml) contains ten crates. The graph shows
+a **subset of Linux build dependencies** read from their manifests, not authorization
+flow or a set of deployed services.
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart TB
+    CLI["swarm-cli<br/>swarm-rust binary"] --> WEB["swarm-web<br/>Native HTTP boundary"]
+    CLI --> ENGINE["swarm-engine<br/>RootStore and business contracts"]
+    WEB --> ENGINE
+    CLI --> BOOT["swarm-enrollment-<br/>bootstrap<br/>Installation observation"]
+    ENGINE --> ID["swarm-identity-contract<br/>Data validation"]
+    ENGINE --> WIRE["swarm-wire-json<br/>Encoding compatibility"]
+    WEB --> ID
+    WEB --> WIRE
+    classDef entry fill:#fffefa,stroke:#205e70,color:#062b49,stroke-width:2px;
+    classDef core fill:#062b49,stroke:#062b49,color:#fffefa,stroke-width:2px;
+    classDef data fill:#f5f3ec,stroke:#926300,color:#243d4a,stroke-width:2px;
+    class CLI,WEB entry;
+    class ENGINE core;
+    class BOOT,ID,WIRE data;
+```
+
+| Source | Role and limitation |
+| --- | --- |
+| [swarm-cli](../../rust/crates/swarm-cli/src/lib.rs) | Decode and render native commands; never call the Go engine |
+| [swarm-web](../../rust/crates/swarm-web/src/lib.rs) | HTTP boundary, sessions and connected native routes; incomplete Go replacement |
+| [swarm-engine](../../rust/crates/swarm-engine/src/lib.rs) | Models, transitions, planning, execution, supervision, checks and settings within the ported scope |
+| [RootStore](../../rust/crates/swarm-engine/src/root_store.rs) | Project and persisted-settings access; neither human authentication nor permission to share a live Go root |
+| [swarm-identity-contract](../../rust/crates/swarm-identity-contract/src/lib.rs) | Identity data validation; valid data does not authenticate a principal |
+| [swarm-enrollment-proof](../../rust/crates/swarm-enrollment-proof/src/lib.rs) | Signed proofs compatible with the Go format; signing bytes grants no business rights |
+| [swarm-enrollment-state](../../rust/crates/swarm-enrollment-state/src/lib.rs) | Native signed journal; trusted anchoring and freshness at final use remain separate obligations |
+| [swarm-enrollment-authority](../../rust/crates/swarm-enrollment-authority/src/lib.rs) | Versioned authority documents; payloads are not execution capabilities |
+| [swarm-enrollment-config](../../rust/crates/swarm-enrollment-config/src/lib.rs) | Installation configuration and protected local storage; no proof of an authenticated operator |
+| [swarm-enrollment-bootstrap](../../rust/crates/swarm-enrollment-bootstrap/src/lib.rs) | Declaration and Linux observation; human labels, keys or distinct UIDs do not establish authority |
+| [swarm-wire-json](../../rust/crates/swarm-wire-json/src/lib.rs) | Shared encoding behavior; each protocol retains its schema and canonicality rules |
+
+Presentation assets live in `web/`, `frontend/` and `locales/`. CLI and HTTP
+consume engine operations through their own input and output boundaries. Actual
+served assets, build profile and exercised binary must be checked for each
+delivery; testing workspace files alone does not establish their inclusion in
+an executable.
+
+## From a plan to a supervised attempt
+
+This flow presents the shared logical contract. The plan lists native branches
+actually verified; the diagram closes neither G1/G3 nor remaining review,
+validation and interface integrations.
+
+```mermaid
+sequenceDiagram
+    participant S as Supervisor
+    participant E as Engine / RootStore
+    participant D as Durable state
+    participant W as Provider attempt
+    participant V as Checks / review
+    S->>E: Proposal bound to received context
+    E->>D: Check scope, revision, lease and preconditions
+    alt Start refused
+        E-->>S: Structured refusal and safe cause
+    else Start authorized
+        E->>D: Reserve and retain the intention
+        E->>W: Launch the authorized attempt
+        W-->>E: Activity, result or incident
+        E->>D: Retain observations and known state
+        E-->>S: Deliver facts and uncertainty
+        S->>E: Next-step decision within authority
+        E->>V: Examine candidate and evidence
+        V-->>E: Candidate-bound results and opinion
+        E-->>S: State after verified application
+    end
+    Note over S,V: Process completion does not establish acceptance
+```
+
+Duration, silence and tool waits are observations. Requested and observed stops
+are distinct. An error may follow a write: it does not prove no mutation occurred.
+Uncertain effects must be reconciled before retry; historical usage and evidence
+are preserved. The conductor and worker supervision have separate lifecycles:
+the conductor ending does not establish termination of workers already released.
+
+Contracts: [supervision](RUN-SUPERVISION.md), [worker admission](NATIVE-MISSION-WORKER.md),
+[lease maintenance](NATIVE-MISSION-CYCLE.md), [reviewer](NATIVE-REVIEWER.md),
+[global judge](NATIVE-GLOBAL-JUDGE.md). The native global judge has scoped proofs
+for `continue`/`renew`; `judge/end` remains refused under its current contract.
+A ported reviewer component does not establish complete `mission watch` integration.
+
+## Identity and memory
+
+Identity separates **initiating principal, logical agent and execution instance**.
+The contract binds grants to scope, revision, content and delegation, expiry and
+revocation conditions. Digests bind data; they authenticate neither a human nor
+a future effect. Enrollment components, process observations and web sessions
+must remain distinct from final business authority. The [identity contract](AGENT-IDENTITY-CONTRACT.md)
+retains outstanding public integration and protected human-authority requirements.
+
+[![Historical Go memory and pending identity integration](../diagrams/memory-identity-en.svg)](../diagrams/memory-identity-en.svg)
+
+Memory follows **verified lessons learned → admission → version → explicit
+selection → received context** in the historical Go foundation. Versions,
+sources, conditions and already received contexts are preserved. Withdrawal
+affects future selection without erasing prompts already delivered to providers.
+Global `read`, `summarize` and `transmit` enforcement remains pending; the Rust
+G8 project/memory journey is open. See [memory](PROJECT-MEMORY.md) and the
+[usage contract, FR](../plans/deepagents-integration/CONTRAT-USAGES-MEMOIRE.md).
+
+## Two interfaces and future security
+
+The [product decision, FR](../PRODUCT-ARCHITECTURE.md) plans **Projects and
+development** and **Business processes** over a shared engine, with separately
+buildable and deployable frontends. Proposed routes, a complete business UX and
+external effects are not declared delivered. A billing simulation authorizes
+no real payment.
+
+The [trusted actions target](ACTIONS-CONFIANCE.md) and [AC-02 plan](plans/actions-confiance/securite-execution-apex.md)
+cover Linux confinement, TCP/REST networking, secrets, lineage evidence, recovery
+and menus. **AC-02 A0–A7 is saved, not started.** Its four views are the policy
+editor, blocked actions, connection lineage and security timeline. The intended
+OpenShell subset must be explicit and verified; Agent Baseline YAML files are
+control catalogues, not executable confinement. Sources and versions are retained
+in the plan.
+
+## Evidence status and reading guidance
+
+| Domain | Status to retain |
+| --- | --- |
+| Historical Go | Functional reference for documented journeys; no evidence of native parity |
+| Rust | Verified components and scoped journeys; overall coverage, installation and cutover remain open |
+| Identity and memory | Documented foundations and protocols; global public protection and memory parity are unproven |
+| Two UX applications and AC-02 | Retained targets; complete separability and confinement are not declared available |
+
+Proofs 213/224/244 cited in the [explainer video](../communication/linkedin-swarm-identite-memoire-20261023/video/README.md)
+use fixture providers; the video does not record the application. For current
+status, follow the active plan rather than infer qualification from an old
+chronology. This documentation overview changes no binary, setting, service,
+agent context or mission.
